# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the values may not apply
#   to the users of the library. However, for an application, you might want to track them.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if delegates have different python versions passed,
#   Pipfile.lock might cause conflicts.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains specific versions of dependencies
#   and may be optionally ignored.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains specific versions of dependencies
#   and may be optionally ignored.
# pdm.lock

